    "text": "Let us consider a curve, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced></math> passing through the point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;and the slope of the tangent to the curve at any point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>)</mo></math> is given by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>+</mo><mi>x</mi><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>&#39;</mo></msup><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>.</mo></math>&nbsp;Then"
